#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0367 expect=skipped domain=ADSL
#note "THE SHAPE THIS PLAN GATES. ADSL carries NO ACTARM while DM does; before the declaration the absent column folded to a broadcast \"\" and differed from DM.ACTARM on every row. Verdict 2-2, NOT 2-1': ACTARM is Permissible in ADSL at ADaMIG 1.1/1.2/1.3 (and not published at all at 1.0, which is why this rule does not ship into rules-cdisc-adamig-1-0), so its absence is NOT a finding and NO reporter is owed -- by ruling, nothing else reports it. Skipping is the whole answer here."
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SAFFL   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | Y
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col ACTARM  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | Placebo
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 | Placebo
---
